/* book exam traps: Sign slip: resting potential is negative inside; writing +70 mV reverses the cell. | Threshold is a depolarised voltage near −55 mV, not the resting voltage; a stimulus below threshold does not fire. | All-or-none: a stronger stimulus increases firing rate, not spike height. | Unit slip: mV and ms are thousandths; 100 mV = 0.1 V, and 2 ms = 0.002 s. | Spike amplitude is peak minus rest (100 mV here), not peak minus threshold (85 mV). Peak-to-peak runs from the highest to the lowest point, so for this trace it includes the undershoot and is 110 mV. */
